  "summary": "A gas turbine works on the Brayton cycle: an axial compressor squeezes air, fuel is burned in the combustors at nearly constant pressure, and the hot gas expands through the turbine. The turbine drives the compressor and has power left over for a generator or compressor. The hot exhaust is often used in a heat-recovery boiler (combined cycle).",
